    "description": "Artist Unknown\nBlack Forest Bear Tray & Pensive Christ Shrine\nHand-Carved Wood, Twigs, and Straw\n12\" H x 8.2\" W (Lot)\nUnsigned\nThis vintage folk art collection includes two distinct hand-carved wood pieces: a Black Forest style desk tray with a carved standing bear, pen groove, and lidded box, alongside an Eastern European wayside shrine depicting the Pensive Christ (Chrystus Frasobliwy) beneath a thatched canopy of twigs and straw.\nBlack Forest desk organizer features gouged fur textures and rustic log styling\nDevotional wayside shrine showcases traditional regional folk carving techniques\nHand-assembled natural materials including bark-on twigs and bound reed canopy\nCondition:\nGood vintage condition overall with age-appropriate wear. Bear tray shows minor surface scuffs, light timber aging, and adhesive traces around feet. Shrines shows light bending to straw thatch and natural wood drying checks.\nOverall Condition\n: All items are USED and are sold AS-IS. Please open a ticket for any questions prior to bidding.\nUsed Item Description\n: Used condition indicates item(s) show signs of regular use, age and may have had repairs or may need repairs. All items featured are DONATED and all sales are FINAL. All BIDS are placed by the buyer with the understanding that this is a donated item that may contain faults unseen by our staff and is ultimately SOLD AS-IS as all information is presented. Items come strictly as pictured and should be assumed to be AS-IS with possible unseen defects. We are\nNOT\nexperts in any field.",
