    "description": "Missouri Meerschaum / Hirschl & Bendheim\nCorn Cob Pipe Wood Display Plaque\nHardwood, Brass, Corn Cob, Approximately 7.25 x 5 Inches\nVintage tobacciana display plaque celebrating Washington, Missouri's historic legacy as the corn cob pipe capital of the world. The finished dark wood mount features an engraved brass plaque titled \"An American Heritage - the original Missouri Meerschaum Corn Cob Pipe,\" paired with an authentic corn cob pipe held securely by a metal spring clip. The pipe's bowl retains its original green Hirschl & Bendheim factory label on the underside, representing one of Missouri Meerschaum's most storied historical contemporaries.\nBeveled dark-stained wood display plaque with black metal spring retaining clip\nEngraved brass nameplate featuring the official Missouri Meerschaum company seal\nCorn cob pipe featuring a textured shank, metal ferrule, and amber-colored bit\nOriginal green paper label on pipe base marked Hirschl & Bendheim, Washington, Missouri\nPlaque measures approximately 7.25 inches wide by 5 inches tall\nCondition:\nWood plaque is structurally sound with light edge wear and minor finish scuffs. Brass plate is securely attached with light surface patina. Pipe shows bowl interior darkening and charring consistent with prior use. Exterior cob bowl and amber stem show light handling wear. Underside factory sticker is intact and legible.",
